     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: New transmission lines constructed 
Indicator: Three new 220 kV transmission lines 70 km each (total 216 km) constructed and is operational by 2016 (target year) 
Achievement: 0 
Progress/Status: Lot 1: PDSI contract between BT and Kalpataru-Jyoti Consortium was signed on 11 February 2013 and became effective on 1 April 2013. On 10 July 2015, the contract completion date was extended till 10 December 2016 (by 17 months) to include the construction of new 220kV Sughd-Kairakkum TL (65 km).

220kV Kairakum - Asht transmission line (74.0 km) was energized in May 2015.
220kV Geran 2 - Rumi transmission line (77.3 km) was energized in December 2016.
220kV Kairakum - Sughd transmission line (65.9 km) was energized in April 2017.
 
Data Source: Barki Tojik annual reports

Barki Tojik Commissioning Certificates</narrative>
